MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Queen and Fleetwood Mac feel like natural next choices after my classic rock hits listening because I want memorable songs collected in one album.",
    "Frankie Valli & The 4 Seasons especially appeals to me because it connects with my interest in mid-sixties songs, reflected in AM Gold and my older hits collections."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour does not fit my wish to revisit older hits today; my earlier interest in newer pop does not make it a priority on this visit.",
    "Title and It's the Girls! give me too little information to connect them to songs or artists I want. Chronicle's greatest-hits format appeals to me, but I am unsure whose music it contains."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A best-of collection is appealing, but that format alone does not make every artist an equally strong choice for me.",
    "My interest in pop across different eras seems to have been treated too broadly; today I am leaning toward familiar older songs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The mid-sixties connection matters especially strongly to me, which makes Frankie Valli & The 4 Seasons stand out among otherwise suitable collections.",
    "I choose selectively even among good matches: Hall & Oates, Eagles and Supertramp fit my interests, but I would leave them for another visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations largely understood my interest in older hits collections, but missed which eras and artists make me want to listen now."
}
